    "title": "Hillsborough County approves $95 million plan to tackle flooding and drainage issues - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Jason Lanning ,\n19 hours ago TAMPA, Fla. — Hillsborough County commissioners have signed off on an ambitious set of stormwater improvement projects aimed at reducing flooding and strengthening infrastructure across the region. The plan includes 10 projects with a total cost of $95 million, funded through a federal community block grant for disaster recovery... Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 1",
